CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
As array_rf_conditional_update, asserting only what holds: when p points into
a, the thread joined has written 5 at a[1]. A read-from that dropped the
conditional update, or never let its condition hold, reads the 0 written
before and reports a violation the program does not have. Checked by never
letting the condition hold in the selection.
